# H1a (SOFT, card M only, FIRST): the HANG PASS of H1, the one-card sub-device overlap harness (optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/subdev_h1.py), under the watcher. One chip, two command queues, ONE
# sub-device manager with an 80-core TARGET sub-device and a 30-core DRAFTER sub-device (whole columns of the reported compute grid), a ~400-op target-like trace (matmuls, activations, products and
# residual adds shaped like a 64-row verify slice) captured on queue 0 and a ~900-op drafter-like trace on queue 1 (and the drafter again on queue 0, the one-queue control, since a trace replays only on
# the queue it was captured on). WATCHER=1 sets TT_METAL_WATCHER=5 and runs the harness --no-timing: few rounds, every replay arm (target alone, drafter alone, both concurrently, chained by an event,
# both on one queue) exactly as the timed pass runs them, every compared op output byte for byte against the solo runs. The watcher distorts every wall, so NO timing is judged here: it asks only
# whether the two queues can be in flight together without a NoC sanitiser trip, a sub-device ownership error or a hang (a per-call watchdog exits 3 on a hang, with a faulthandler backstop).
# READ: the line 'SUBDEV_H1 verdict=UNTIMED-PASS' (bytes identical, nothing hung); the script prints the watcher log's error/assert line count after the run and the watcher log is in the results.
# STOP on FAIL-BYTES, NOT-MEASURED (the error text is in the line: a TT_FATAL here is the answer to 'does this tt-metal accept the construction'), a hang (exit 3, 124 or 137: reset THE TARGET CARD only,
# the script prints the command) or any watcher error line: H1b is then skipped (ORDER.txt NEEDS). Duration (estimate): 30 min (the attach and the kernel compile are most of it; the container timeout is 45 min).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env): this pack builds nothing, and any C2 image carries the tt-metal sub-device bindings
# it needs (the harnesses mount this checkout's files). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 WATCHER=1
